IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `taslsl-dates`
IMPORT `taslsl-employee`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1976 (Tas) -- worked cases for the employee's questions (taslsl-employee.l4), the deadline rule
-- and the date helpers. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (consolidation published
-- 2025-01-22); none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts,
-- not about the law; the facts are illustrative. Breached traces are asserted through the question (CONSIDER EVALTRACE
-- ... WHEN FULFILLED inside), and the rule itself is #TRACEd with "-- expect:" lines.
-- Edges: 10 years and 9.99; 14, 15, 19, 20 years (ss 8(2)(a), 8A(2)(a)); 7 and 6.99, 5 and 4.99 (ss 8(2)(b), 8A(2)(b));
-- exactly 10 at death (s 9(2)(a) "more than 10"); 32 hours and 31.5 (s 5(3)); 3 months and a day over from 15 March and
-- 30 November (s 5(1)(g), 5(9)); 6 months and a day over, 14 days and a day over (s 5(1)(h)); 2 months from 31 August
-- (s 2(2)); 6 months from 31 August (s 12(1)(a)); 8 2/3 weeks and 8.6, 4 1/3 and 4.3, 13 and 12.9 (s 12(10)); 60 and
-- 59, 65 and 64 (s 2 "age for retirement"); the due day and the day after, a part payment, a due day of 0 days
-- (s 12(4), (6)(a)); 3 years and a day over from 10 March and 29 February (s 15(1)); a zero divisor (s 11).
-- Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `is a leap year` 2024
#ASSERT (NOT (`is a leap year` 2100))
#ASSERT `the same day` 1 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2025
#ASSERT `the same day` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `the same day` (0 MINUS 3) `years after` (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2023
#ASSERT `the completed years from` (`d` 1 7 2015) `to` (`d` 30 6 2025) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the completed years from` (`d` 1 7 2015) `to` (`d` 29 6 2025) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the completed years from` (`d` 1 7 2015) `to` (`d` 1 7 2015) EQUALS 0

§§ `ss 2, 3, 7 -- does the Act apply`

#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies to me`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: I am not employed by an employer for hire or reward, nor an apprentice, so I am not an employee (s 2(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: I am a State employee under the Long Service Leave (State Employees) Act 1994 (s 3(a))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply to me: I am entitled to long service leave under the Local Government (Building and Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1993 (s 3(c))`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Act applies to me, but the Secretary has exempted my employer for employees like me because a long service leave scheme gives benefits no less favourable (s 7)`

§§ `ss 2, 2A, Schedule 2 -- mining employee`

#ASSERT `Am I a mining employee` TRUE `a place, open cut, quarry, shaft, tunnel or other excavation where a mineral substance is obtained` Gold EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a mining employee` TRUE `a place where 2 or more people are employed prospecting or exploring for a mineral substance` Nickel EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a mining employee` TRUE `the surface, buildings, workshops or works around such a mine, occupied with it for working it` `Tungsten and its ores` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a mining employee` TRUE `a place, open cut, quarry, shaft, tunnel or other excavation where a mineral substance is obtained` `a substance not listed in Schedule 2 (for example coal, limestone, gravel or sand)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a mining employee` TRUE `none of these` Tin EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a mining employee` FALSE `a place next to such a mine where its product is stacked, stored, crushed or treated` Zinc EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 2(2), 5 -- continuous employment`

-- 1 July 2015 to 31 December 2025: 10 years and 184 days of a 365-day year.
#ASSERT `How many years of continuous employment do I have` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 31 12 2025) 0 EQUALS 10 PLUS (184 DIVIDED BY 365)
#ASSERT `How many years of continuous employment do I have` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 30 6 2025) 0 EQUALS 10
-- 30 days not counted: the start moves to 31 July 2015; to 30 June 2025 is 9 years and 335 of 365 days.
#ASSERT `How many years of continuous employment do I have` (`d` 1 7 2015) (`d` 30 6 2025) 30 EQUALS 9 PLUS (335 DIVIDED BY 365)

#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `illness or injury, certified as necessary by a medical practitioner` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 9 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `an industrial dispute` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 4 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `an industrial dispute` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 4 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 5(1)(g): ended 15 March 2025; 15 June 2025 is the last day.
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `my employment ended for a reason other than slackness of trade, and the same employer re-employed me` FALSE (`d` 15 3 2025) (`d` 15 6 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `my employment ended for a reason other than slackness of trade, and the same employer re-employed me` FALSE (`d` 15 3 2025) (`d` 16 6 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- From 30 November 2024, 3 months end on 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `my employment ended for a reason other than slackness of trade, and the same employer re-employed me` FALSE (`d` 30 11 2024) (`d` 28 2 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `my employment ended for a reason other than slackness of trade, and the same employer re-employed me` FALSE (`d` 30 11 2024) (`d` 1 3 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 5(1)(h): stood down 1 January 2025; back by 1 July 2025 and within 14 days of the offer.
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `I was stood down, or my employment ended, because of slackness of trade, and I returned` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 7 2025) (`d` 20 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `I was stood down, or my employment ended, because of slackness of trade, and I returned` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 2 7 2025) (`d` 20 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `I was stood down, or my employment ended, because of slackness of trade, and I returned` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 17 4 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `I was stood down, or my employment ended, because of slackness of trade, and I returned` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 16 4 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `service in the naval, military or air forces of the Commonwealth, other than the permanent forces` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Did the break keep my employment continuous` `something else (for example an absence without my employer's leave)` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2025) (`d` 1 5 2025) (`d` 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Does the break count towards my years` `illness or injury, certified as necessary by a medical practitioner` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the break count towards my years` `jury service, or appearing before a court or other body as a witness or a party` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the break count towards my years` `maternity leave, in accordance with my terms of employment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the break count towards my years` `an industrial dispute` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the break count towards my years` `another absence with my employer's leave (for example unpaid leave)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the break count towards my years` `something else (for example an absence without my employer's leave)` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `As a casual or part-time worker am I continuously employed` TRUE 32 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `As a casual or part-time worker am I continuously employed` TRUE 31.5 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `As a casual or part-time worker am I continuously employed` FALSE 40 EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `the business I worked in was transferred to my present employer (sold, assigned or passed on) and I became its employee` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `I transferred from one corporation to a related corporation` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 1 1 2021) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 2(2): ended 31 August 2025; 2 months end on 31 October 2025.
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `my job ended and another employer took me on at the same place, in the same or substantially the same kind of business` (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 31 10 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `my job ended and another employer took me on at the same place, in the same or substantially the same kind of business` (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 1 11 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 5(9): apprenticeship completed 30 November 2025; 3 months end on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `I finished my apprenticeship with this employer and it kept me on` (`d` 30 11 2025) (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `I finished my apprenticeship with this employer and it kept me on` (`d` 30 11 2025) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does my earlier service count` `none of these` (`d` 1 1 2020) (`d` 2 1 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE

