§§ `s 11 -- ordinary pay`

-- A fixed rate of $30 an hour, 38 fixed hours: $1,140; with board and lodging worth $50 a week: $1,190.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` `my terms fix an ordinary rate for my work` 30 0 0 TRUE 38 0 0 EQUALS JUST 1140
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` `my terms fix an ordinary rate for my work` 30 0 0 TRUE 38 0 50 EQUALS JUST 1190
-- No hours fixed: 1,560 hours in 12 months / 52 = 30 hours; at $30: $900.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` `my terms fix an ordinary rate for my work` 30 0 0 FALSE 0 1560 0 EQUALS JUST 900
-- Results: $10,400 for 520 hours in 3 months = $20 an hour; 38 hours: $760.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` `my pay depends on the results I achieve` 0 10400 520 TRUE 38 0 0 EQUALS JUST 760
-- No rate fixed: $52,000 for 2,080 hours in 12 months = $25 an hour; no hours fixed: 2,080 / 52 = 40 hours: $1,000.
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` `no ordinary rate is fixed for my work` 0 52000 2080 FALSE 0 2080 0 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `What is my weekly ordinary pay` `my pay depends on the results I achieve` 0 10400 0 TRUE 38 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 12(4) -- when my employment ends`

-- 12 years, resigned, $1,000 a week: 10.4 weeks = $10,400.
#ASSERT `What must I be paid when my employment ends` FALSE 12 `I resigned or retired for another reason` FALSE 0 1000 EQUALS 10400
#ASSERT `What must I be paid when my employment ends` FALSE 12 `I am still employed` FALSE 0 1000 EQUALS 0
-- 8 years, dismissed other than for misconduct, $1,500 a week: 104/15 weeks = $10,400.
#ASSERT `What must I be paid when my employment ends` FALSE 8 `my employer ended it for a reason other than my serious and wilful misconduct` FALSE 0 1500 EQUALS 10400
-- Mining, 12 years, resigned, $1,000: 15.6 weeks = $15,600.
#ASSERT `What must I be paid when my employment ends` TRUE 12 `I resigned or retired for another reason` FALSE 0 1000 EQUALS 15600
-- 17 years, 13 weeks taken, $900: (221/15 - 13) = 26/15 weeks = $1,560.
#ASSERT `What must I be paid when my employment ends` FALSE 17 `I resigned or retired for another reason` FALSE 13 900 EQUALS 1560

§§ `s 9 -- on a death`

-- 12 years, still employed: s 9(1) 26/3 + s 9(2)(a) 2 x 52/60 = 26/15; total 156/15 = 10.4 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` FALSE 12 TRUE 0 EQUALS 10.4
-- Exactly 10 years: s 9(1) 26/3; s 9(2)(a) needs "more than 10", (b) "less than 10".
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` FALSE 10 TRUE 0 EQUALS 26 DIVIDED BY 3
-- 8 years: s 9(2)(b) 8 x 52/60 = 104/15.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` FALSE 8 TRUE 0 EQUALS 104 DIVIDED BY 15
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` FALSE 6.5 TRUE 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` FALSE 8 FALSE 0 EQUALS 0
-- 16 years, 13 weeks taken: s 9(1) 0; s 9(2)(a) 1 x 52/60 = 13/15.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` FALSE 16 TRUE 13 EQUALS 13 DIVIDED BY 15
-- Mining: 12 years 13 + 2 x 52/40 = 15.6; 6 years 6 x 52/40 = 7.8; 4 years 0.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` TRUE 12 TRUE 0 EQUALS 15.6
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` TRUE 6 TRUE 0 EQUALS 7.8
#ASSERT `How many weeks of pay are owed to the estate` TRUE 4 TRUE 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much must be paid to the estate` FALSE 12 TRUE 0 1000 0 EQUALS 10400
#ASSERT `How much must be paid to the estate` FALSE 12 TRUE 0 1000 2000 EQUALS 8400
#ASSERT `How much must be paid to the estate` FALSE 8 TRUE 0 1500 0 EQUALS 10400

§§ `s 12(4), (6)(a) -- paid on time`

-- Leave fixed 1 March 2026 to begin 1 May 2026 (61 days).
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) 5000 5000 (`d` 1 5 2026) (`d` 10 5 2026) EQUALS `paid in full on time`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) 5000 5000 (`d` 2 5 2026) (`d` 10 5 2026) EQUALS `paid in full, but late`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) 5000 5000 (`d` 1 2 2026) (`d` 10 5 2026) EQUALS `paid in full on time`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) 5000 4999 (`d` 30 4 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet paid in full, and not yet due`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 5 2026) 5000 4999 (`d` 30 4 2026) (`d` 2 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet paid in full, and overdue`
-- Employment ended 30 June 2026: due that day.
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 30 6 2026) (`d` 30 6 2026) 10400 10400 (`d` 30 6 2026) (`d` 10 7 2026) EQUALS `paid in full on time`
#ASSERT `Was my leave pay paid on time` (`d` 30 6 2026) (`d` 30 6 2026) 10400 10400 (`d` 1 7 2026) (`d` 10 7 2026) EQUALS `paid in full, but late`

-- The rule itself, on a timeline in days.
#TRACE `s 12(4), (6)(a) -- pay the leave in full when it begins` 5000 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `pay my long service leave` 5000 AT 61
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 12(4), (6)(a) -- pay the leave in full when it begins` 5000 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `pay my long service leave` 5000 AT 62
-- expect: BREACH by my employer (paid on day 62, after the day 61 deadline)
#TRACE `s 12(4), (6)(a) -- pay the leave in full when it begins` 5000 61 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `my employer` DOES `pay my long service leave` 4000 AT 30
    (WAITUNTIL 62)
-- expect: BREACH by my employer (a part payment does not count; 61 days pass)

§§ `ss 13, 14A, 15, 20, 21 -- disputes, recovery and prosecution`

#ASSERT `Can I refer my dispute` `whether or when I am, or became, entitled to long service leave or payment instead of it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
